# `bt` core

`bt` is problem-independent balanced-ternary mathematics.

```python
# BAD
from research.residuals.cubic_fibres import fibre_of

# GOOD — closed form stays in core
from bt.calculus.cubic import F_k, cubic_residual_formula, prefixes_at
```

Stay in `bt.calculus`: trit, `D` / `I_a`, rewrite, VM, section, jets, residual `≡_k`, `poly_congruence`, quadratic, and the **entire** `cubic.py` (`F_k`, prefix helpers).

Leave `bt.calculus.__init__` as the general façade (trit, `D`/`I`, jets, `hatD`). Do not re-export fibres, layers, `N1`/`N0`, or `Q`.

`is_prime` / `factorize` live on `bt.arithmetic`, not the `bt` package façade.

A new core fact needs a unit test under `tests/unit/` and a ledger row when it is a named theorem.
